text:
daria: quick accessibility sweep of the time-series chart legend (right rail). Found a few issues: legend swatches aren't keyboard focusable, SR reads raw SVG markup, and color-only toggles are hard for color-blind users.

sam: thanks  which browser/AT and repro steps?

daria: NVDA+Firefox. Tab into chart area -> can't reach legend items. Clicking swatch toggles series visibility visually, but screen reader just says 'graphics' or reads path data because we used bare SVG groups. Also the small 10px swatch contrast vs background is poor.

a11y-bot: Auto-check results: legend swatches not focusable (FAIL), SVG has no accessible name (WARN), contrast check: swatch border too low (2.6:1 FAIL for control), color contrast between series colors (pairwise) may be ambiguous for color-deficient users.

mike: we rendered legend as <svg><g>...</g></svg> for pixel-perfect look. We can keep visuals but expose interactive controls via <button> overlays or recreate legend as list of native buttons. Prefer semantic HTML for keyboard/support.

hana: agree. recommended pattern: <ul role=\"list\"><li><button aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"Toggle series Sales: currently visible\"> <span class=\"swatch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> Sales</button></li></ul>. Use aria-pressed to indicate toggled state and update it on click. Provide an offscreen sr-only description for more context.

oliver: also consider aria-live updates: when a series is toggled, announce "Series Sales hidden" in a polite live region. But avoid double announcements if the visual chart also updates via DOM changes.

daria: proposed fixes: 1) rebuild legend as accessible list + buttons 2) add aria-pressed and update on toggle 3) add sr-only status text and a role=\"status\" live region to announce changes 4) increase swatch visible size/border to meet 3:1 and provide patterned fills for color-blindness 5) ensure keyboard arrow navigation between legend items (Left/Right or Up/Down) for quicker switching.

sam: paste minimal markup + CSS + small JS so I can drop into chart component.

daria: sure, quick example:

```html
<!-- accessible legend markup -->
<ul class=\"chart-legend\" role=\"list\">
  <li>
    <button class=\"legend-btn\" aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"Toggle series Sales, currently visible\" data-series=\"sales\">
      <span class=\"swatch\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"background:#1f77b4\"></span>
      <span class=\"label\">Sales</span>
      <span class=\"sr-only\">Visible</span>
    </button>
  </li>
</ul>
<div id=\"chart-announcer\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"sr-only\" aria-atomic=\"true\"></div>
```

```css
.legend-btn { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:none; border:none; padding:6px; font:inherit; }
.legend-btn:focus-visible { outline:3px solid #ffb74d; outline-offset:3px; border-radius:4px; }
.swatch { width:14px; height:14px; border:2px solid #0f172a; border-radius:3px; }
.sr-only { position:absolute !important; width:1px; height:1px; padding:0; margin:-1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0,0,0,0); white-space:nowrap; border:0; }
```

```js
// toggling + keyboard nav
const buttons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.legend-btn'));
buttons.forEach((btn,i)=>{
  btn.addEventListener('click', ()=>{
    const pressed = btn.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
    btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(!pressed));
    const series = btn.dataset.series;
    document.getElementById('chart-announcer').textContent = `${series} ${pressed ? 'hidden' : 'visible'}`;
    // call chart.toggleSeries(series)
  });
  btn.addEventListener('keydown', (e)=>{
    if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'ArrowDown') buttons[(i+1)%buttons.length].focus();
    if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'ArrowUp') buttons[(i-1+buttons.length)%buttons.length].focus();
    if (e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'Enter') { e.preventDefault(); btn.click(); }
  });
});
```

mike: nice. A few notes: 1) ensure the sr-only text "Visible/Hidden" is kept in sync but avoid duplicating info in aria-label to prevent verbosity; instead aria-label can be "Toggle series Sales" and the aria-pressed conveys state. 2) for charts with many series, allow Shift+Click to isolate one series (visual UX) but don't force SR verbosity. 3) patterned fills: include a CSS background-image for swatch when color palettes are ambiguous.

hana: testing plan: run axe-core, NVDA/VO manual check to ensure screen reader announces toggles, test keyboard arrow navigation, verify live region announces only one line per action, and take colorblindness sim screenshots. Add unit tests asserting aria-pressed toggles and chart-announcer text updates.

daria: I'll open a small PR with the component refactor + axe results + screenshots. PR summary: "Make chart legend accessible: semantic buttons, aria-pressed state, visible focus, live region announcements, patterned fills for color-deficiency, and arrow-key navigation." Tagging @sam for review. :raised_hands:
